WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.330
Speaker 1: Very interesting news on the cannabis
front.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:09.549
The House of Representatives yesterday passed
a law which would allow banks to provide services

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:15.769
to cannabis companies in states where it is
legal, which is a significant step towards

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:20.689
removing what is a real barrier to the development
of this industry nationally.

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:26.109
As we've talked about before, there has been
a major issue within the cannabis space where

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:34.660
even if it is legal and illegal, that could
be recreational, illegal, recreationally decriminalized,

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:35.660
but medically legal.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.150
And so that's what the pot shops essentially
are selling.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.890
Whatever the case, if you have to deal in
cash because banks aren't allowed to work

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.399
with you, that is a major problem.

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:49.180
It's a security problem because people know
you have so much cash around.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.719
It's a problem in a lot of different ways.

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:57.789
Lawmakers voted 321 to 101, which means Democrats,
but also some Republicans to approve the bill

00:00:57.789 --> 00:00:59.449
and send it to the Senate.

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:04.500
It is unclear what is going to happen in the
Senate, but we know that banks have been generally

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.400
not willing to do business with companies
that are in this business because they could

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.260
be running afoul of federal laws.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:18.119
Now, I'm aware because I have friends in the
industry in, let's say in in Arizona, in Massachusetts

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:24.320
and some other states, they've told me that
there are credit unions that operate only

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:30.630
within one state that seem more willing to
work with cannabis dispensaries and other

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.940
businesses, and they feel relatively comfortable
that the government is not going to go after

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:35.940
them.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.610
I don't know whether that's actually true
or not.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.310
I don't know if that's a false sense of security.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.170
But this is a really important thing.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:48.780
Now, where you get to a conflict is the banking
industry wants this.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.780
And why do they want it?

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.220
Well, because it will be hugely profitable.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.620
And there is a contingent of people who are
sort of stuck between what is seemingly a

00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.540
rock and a hard place for them where they
want cannabis legalization, but they really

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.380
are skeptical of the banking industry.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:06.770
So if the banking industry wants something,
their reflexive reaction is to be against

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.770
it.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.100
Listen, banks are going to make money with
this.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.500
Banks are going to make money with anything
that is, you know, whether it's IPOs of companies

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.330
that shouldn't be going or holding money for
arms deals, banks are going to make money

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.330
regardless.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:27.620
The question is, do we want to further legitimize
this as an industry so that we can get away

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:34.410
from spending tax money, imprisoning people
who either use, have or sell marijuana and

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:39.250
rather collect tax money from this as a regulated
industry and be able to use that tax money

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.560
for public health initiatives, for education,
for whatever the case may be.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.450
I'm of the mindset of I don't want my tax
money going to imprison people involved in

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.450
cannabis.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:57.940
I want to see my tax money bolstered for lack
of a better term by tax money from a legal

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.620
and regulated cannabis industry.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.600
My position is clear.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.120
The positions of the United States as a country
are moving more and more in that direction.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.300
This is a big deal.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.310
I don't yet know whether we can expect it
to pass the Senate.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:10.890
We will see

